# Hydri mobile UI

Apply when task is classified `mobile-ui`, `bottom-nav`, `bottom-sheet`, `filter-sheet`, or touches mobile routes.

## Source docs

- `docs/agents/AGENTS-UI-MOBILE-STANDARDS.md`
- `docs/adr/0023-mobile-layout-and-bottom-navigation-pattern.md`
- `.cursor/rules/hydri-ui-architecture.mdc`

## Viewport coverage (mandatory before 🟢)

Test **three widths**: 360×740 (small), 390×844 (standard), 430×932 (large).

Check: overflow horizontal, BottomNav covering content, chips truncated, primary card, safe-area, sheets open/close.

Routes: `/pt-BR/minhas-cargas`, `/pt-BR/cargas` (when in scope).

One width only → 🟡 max, never 🟢.

## Gate (mandatory)

```bash
npm run hydri:gate -- --scope=<scope> --mode=mobile
```

Optional QA scripts when scope includes minhas-cargas:

```bash
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000 node scripts/minhas-cargas-list-premium-qa.mjs
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000 node scripts/minhas-cargas-phase-f-qa.mjs
```

## Proof

Record **Mobile viewport coverage** in `HYDRI_IMPLEMENTATION_PROOF`. Screenshot per width in `output/` is evidence, not source-of-truth — never commit `output/` without approval.

Tests passing ≠ visual OK. Playwright/preview failure = "não validado", not success.
